e different items.\n\n\nThe initial count of 646 was inflated due to duplicate entries across different storage locations, now corrected to 592 unique items. A \"needs review\" category of 140 entries was flagged, initially raising concerns about the rigor of the review process. Manual inspection revealed overly strict matching criteria, particularly regarding dosage forms. The matching logic needs to be relaxed for dosage-form variations.\n\n\n"}
