ة\")**:\n     - User wondered why ~435 items were in `لم يُعثر عليه`.\n  5. **Immediate Question**:\n     - User asks: \"Should I test re-matching now, or restart the program and try re-matching, or are you still editing code?\"\n\n---\n\n## 2. Progress & Completed Work\n\n### Completed:\n1. **Empirical Benchmarking of MSEMAX / ChatGPT Web Payload Limits**:\n   - Built and ran `test_payload_limit.py` and `test_fine_batch.py`:\n     - 300 items (80.1 KB): Failed (`ChatGPT returned 413`).\n     - 150-200 items (40-53 KB): Model triggered code interpreter / summarized output instead of full JSON.\n     - **75-80 items (20-21 KB)**: **100% Success in 11.0s!** Generates clean, full JSON without truncation or 413 errors.\n2. **Optimal Batching & Adaptive 413 Handling (`src/fast_match/coordinator.py`)**:\n   - Replaced batching loops with `batch_size = 75` (reduces messages from 20 down to ~7 batches per warehouse, saving >65% of message quota).\n   - Added automatic split fallback: if any chunk ever hits `413` or payload error, it adaptively splits in half.\n   - Tested live on real data: 134 items processed across 2 batches in **32.5 seconds** with 0 errors.\n3. **Standard Packaging Match Rule (`src/fast_match/coordinator.py`)**:\n   - Updated Rule 3 in `SYSTEM_PROMPT`:\n     - Standard package counts (e.g. `20 قرص`, `5 امبول`, `3 شريط`, `20 فيلم`) matched against standard warehouse entries that don't explicitly specify the count (`ديجستين اقراص/فاركو`, `كيتولاك امبول/العامريه`, `كولونا اقراص`) are now classified as **100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")**, NOT review!\n     - Review is now reserved strictly for explicit numeric conflicts (e.g. 15 tablets vs 60 tablets) or true brand-to-generic substitutions (e.g. Cataflam vs Adwiflam).\n4. **Resolved 646 vs 993 Discrepancy & Refactored Excel Summary (`src/output/excel_writer.py` & `src/fast_match/coordinator.py`)**:\n   - **Root Cause of 993 vs 592**: `0913.xlsx` has 993 customer order rows, but contains only **592 distinct drug names** (e.g. Aspirin Protect repeated 8x, Erythrex 7x, Duricef 7x, Cetal 5x).\n   - **Root Cause of 646**: The old formula `=B3+B4+B5` summed `matched (71) + not_found (435) + review (140) = 646`. Matched was counted per warehouse, so drugs in multiple warehouses were double-counted.\n   - **Fix Applied**:\n     - `ملخص` Row 2: `إجمالي طلبات النواقص (الأسطر)` = 993 (raw input rows).\n     - `ملخص` Row 3: `إجمالي الأصناف الفريدة (المطلوبة)` = 592 (100% baseline).\n     - Rows 4-6: Distinct matched, not found, and review counts without double counting.\n     - `summary` dictionary in `FastCoordinator` sets `total_shortages = len(shortage_items)` (993) and `unique_shortages = len(deduped_shortages)` (592).\n5. **Production Synchronized (`dist_production/`)**:\n   - Ran `scripts/package_production.py` — all changes copied to `dist_production/`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Key Findings & Insights\n- **Why ~435 items are in `لم يُعثر عليه`**:\n  - Direct search in warehouse catalogs confirmed that common shortages in `0913.xlsx` such as `اسبرين بروتكت`, `ابيماج فوار`, `ابيمول لبوس`, and `اوجمانتين` have **0 items** across all 6 warehouse PDF files.\n  - The 6 PDFs are wholesale discount/cash promotions containing only ~1,500 unique items combined, while Egyptian registered pharmaceuticals exceed 17,000. It is normal that two-thirds of the pharmacy's generic shortage list are not found in these specific 6 promotional PDF lists.\n- **Python In-Memory Imports**:\n  - Because `desktop_app/app.py` caches imported modules (`src.fast_match.coordinator` and `src.output.excel_writer`), any code changes require **closing and restarting `desktop_app/app.py`** so Python loads the new prompt rules and summary formatting.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Active Context\n- **Files Modified**:\n  - `src/fast_match/coordinator.py` (75-item batching, 413 fallback, standard pack match rule, 993/592 summary counts).\n  - `src/output/excel_writer.py` (summary sheet rows 2-3 for raw 993 rows and unique 592 drugs)